      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): suppress unhandled stdout/stderr stream errors in execDockerRaw",
        "body": "Re-submission of #100428, which was closed automatically when the active PR queue was limited. The branch has been rebased onto the latest `main`.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`execDockerRaw` attaches `data` listeners to `child.stdout` and `child.stderr`, but does not attach `error` listeners. If either stream emits an `error` event, the unhandled error can crash the OpenClaw process during Docker sandbox operations.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd no-op `error` handlers to both stdout and stderr streams before the data handlers, mirroring the existing `child.on(\"error\", ...)` pattern. This prevents unhandled stream errors from propagating as uncaught exceptions. Also fixes an indentation error in the abort path.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMore robust Docker sandbox operations: transient stream read errors no longer crash the agent runtime.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRegression test:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/sandbox/docker.test.ts\n```\n\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  4 passed (4)\n```\n\nReal behavior proof:\n\n```bash\nnode_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/proof/agents-sandbox-docker-stream-errors.mts\n```\n\nThe proof prepends a fake `docker` binary to PATH, calls the production `execDockerRaw`, and emits real `error` events on the docker child's stdout and stderr streams. With the fix the command still resolves:\n\n```\nDocker exit code: 0\nDocker stdout: {\"status\":\"ok\"}\n\nPASS: stream errors were caught and execDockerRaw still resolved.\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/agents-sandbox-docker-stream-errors",
